{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41718146",
      "title": "Fetching Data By Leveraging NextJS & Fullstack Capabilities",
      "sourceHash": "3502a2ff9778edf24ec1fe26b42160de1be70bae60c7652830b499cc4aac2e6f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.08,
          "end": 3.84,
          "en": "Now when it comes to loading data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.84,
          "end": 5.85,
          "en": "in a NextJS application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.85,
          "end": 8.103,
          "en": "we get a couple of different options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.94,
          "end": 10.89,
          "en": "We could fetch the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.89,
          "end": 15.09,
          "en": "as we would do it in any vanilla React application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.09,
          "end": 19.71,
          "en": "We could, for example, use the useEffect hook like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.71,
          "end": 22.41,
          "en": "and then in there use the fetch function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.41,
          "end": 25.2,
          "en": "to send a request to a backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.2,
          "end": 27.66,
          "en": "And on that backend, we could then reach out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.66,
          "end": 30.03,
          "en": "to that database, which we just set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.03,
          "end": 31.773,
          "en": "and get the data from here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.85,
          "end": 35.19,
          "en": "Now, in a NextJS application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.19,
          "end": 37.95,
          "en": "we actually already have a backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.95,
          "end": 40.26,
          "en": "We have backend and frontend combined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.26,
          "end": 43.14,
          "en": "blended seamlessly together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.14,
          "end": 45.093,
          "en": "So we don't need a separate backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.08,
          "end": 50.28,
          "en": "And as you also learned in NextJS, all your components are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.28,
          "end": 55.28,
          "en": "by default server components that only execute on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.38,
          "end": 58.5,
          "en": "unless you're using a feature that requires them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.5,
          "end": 62.46,
          "en": "to be a client component like useEffect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.46,
          "end": 65.52,
          "en": "But actually, because we have those server components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.52,
          "end": 68.43,
          "en": "as a default, we don't need useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.43,
          "end": 72.15,
          "en": "and we don't need to send a fetch request to get data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.15,
          "end": 75.69,
          "en": "Instead, since this component by default runs on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.69,
          "end": 79.59,
          "en": "and only there, we can directly reach out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.59,
          "end": 81.72,
          "en": "to the database from here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.72,
          "end": 84.351,
          "en": "And that's definitely not something you're used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.351,
          "end": 86.91,
          "en": "to from other React apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.91,
          "end": 90.03,
          "en": "But that's absolutely fine in Next apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.03,
          "end": 92.78999999999999,
          "en": "because this is a server component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.78999999999999,
          "end": 94.71000000000001,
          "en": "that only runs on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.71000000000001,
          "end": 97.983,
          "en": "So reaching out to a database is safe here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.24000000000001,
          "end": 102.21000000000001,
          "en": "Now, in order to keep things separated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.21000000000001,
          "end": 104.85,
          "en": "I'll not write my code in here though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.85,
          "end": 109.59,
          "en": "Instead, I'll add a new folder in my root project folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.59,
          "end": 113.31,
          "en": "which I'll name lib, though that name is up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.31,
          "end": 115.443,
          "en": "and not some kind of reserved name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.55,
          "end": 121.55,
          "en": "But in there I'll add a new file, which I'll name meals.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.62,
          "end": 125.16,
          "en": "And in here I wanna write the code that reaches out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.16,
          "end": 129.12,
          "en": "to a database and gets data from that database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.12,
          "end": 130.32,
          "en": "For that in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.32,
          "end": 135.18,
          "en": "I'll import SQL from this better SQLite three package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135.18,
          "end": 137.82,
          "en": "And I'll then establish the database connection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.82,
          "end": 140.4,
          "en": "by executing SQL as a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.4,
          "end": 143.1,
          "en": "and then passing the name of the database here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.1,
          "end": 145.083,
          "en": "as a string to that function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.25,
          "end": 148.68,
          "en": "And then we can work on this DB object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.68,
          "end": 151.983,
          "en": "to perform actions on that database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 153.51,
          "end": 157.92000000000002,
          "en": "Now for that, I'll add a new exported function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 157.92000000000002,
          "end": 160.14,
          "en": "which I'll name getMeals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 160.14,
          "end": 162.63,
          "en": "which should do what the name implies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 162.63,
          "end": 165.663,
          "en": "It should get all the meals from that database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 166.92000000000002,
          "end": 169.93,
          "en": "And for that we can now use this DB object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 170.79,
          "end": 175.14,
          "en": "and then prepare a new statement, a new SQL statement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 175.14,
          "end": 176.433,
          "en": "that should be executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 177.63,
          "end": 179.94,
          "en": "And here it's a pretty simple statement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 179.94,
          "end": 184.653,
          "en": "I want to select all columns from the meals table.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 187.71,
          "end": 190.871,
          "en": "Then we just have to run this though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 190.871,
          "end": 194.04,
          "en": "you actually don't do that with the run method here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 194.04,
          "end": 195.483,
          "en": "but with the all method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 196.35,
          "end": 199.23,
          "en": "Run would be used if you were inserting data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 199.23,
          "end": 202.23,
          "en": "for example, if you were changing data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 202.23,
          "end": 204.48,
          "en": "all is used if you are fetching data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 204.48,
          "end": 206.52,
          "en": "and you want to get back all the rows",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 206.52,
          "end": 208.953,
          "en": "that are fetched by that statement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 210.57,
          "end": 213.06,
          "en": "If you were looking for a single row,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 213.06,
          "end": 215.57999999999998,
          "en": "you could use get instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 215.57999999999998,
          "end": 218.403,
          "en": "But here it's multiple rows, so it's all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 219.27,
          "end": 222.78,
          "en": "and then we just have to return this result.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 222.78,
          "end": 225.75,
          "en": "This also doesn't yield a promise or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 225.75,
          "end": 228.063,
          "en": "Instead, you can just return it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 228.99,
          "end": 231.63,
          "en": "But speaking of promises, it's worth knowing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 231.63,
          "end": 234.57,
          "en": "and understanding that even though we're not working",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 234.57,
          "end": 235.82999999999998,
          "en": "with promises here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 235.82999999999998,
          "end": 239.49,
          "en": "because the better SQLite three package doesn't use them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 239.49,
          "end": 241.14,
          "en": "even though we're not using them here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 241.14,
          "end": 244.44,
          "en": "we could use them in our component here with ease",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 244.44,
          "end": 248.4,
          "en": "because server component functions can actually be converted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 248.4,
          "end": 250.74,
          "en": "to async functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 250.74,
          "end": 253.86,
          "en": "You can use the async keyword here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 253.86,
          "end": 256.53,
          "en": "something you normally also can't do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 256.53,
          "end": 258.45,
          "en": "on your React components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 258.45,
          "end": 261.51,
          "en": "but you can do it on server components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 261.51,
          "end": 264.78,
          "en": "And if you then had some code that would use a promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 264.78,
          "end": 266.313,
          "en": "you could use await here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 267.57,
          "end": 271.32,
          "en": "And to simulate this, I'll actually go back to Meals.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 271.32,
          "end": 275.04,
          "en": "and turn, getMeals into async function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 275.04,
          "end": 277.11,
          "en": "and therefore, it will return a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 277.11,
          "end": 281.13,
          "en": "even though this code here doesn't normally produce one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 281.13,
          "end": 283.44,
          "en": "but now it will be wrapped into a promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 283.44,
          "end": 285.72,
          "en": "that is what async does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 285.72,
          "end": 288.57,
          "en": "And I'll actually await another promise here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 288.57,
          "end": 291.84000000000003,
          "en": "which simply adds an arbitrary delay,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 291.84000000000003,
          "end": 295.2,
          "en": "just to simulate an action that takes a bit longer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 295.2,
          "end": 298.53,
          "en": "which is something that will help us later once we explore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 298.53,
          "end": 301.44,
          "en": "how we can handle loading states and so on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 301.44,
          "end": 303.033,
          "en": "in Next applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 303.87,
          "end": 306.99,
          "en": "And this is of course not code you would normally add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 306.99,
          "end": 309.96,
          "en": "because you would not want to slow things down,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 309.96,
          "end": 312.12,
          "en": "but here for this demo app, I'll add it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 312.12,
          "end": 314.22,
          "en": "to add this extra delay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 314.22,
          "end": 316.56,
          "en": "And this also allows me to show you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 316.56,
          "end": 319.95,
          "en": "that you can use async await here, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 319.95,
          "end": 321.9,
          "en": "because it's a regular function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 321.9,
          "end": 325.38,
          "en": "but you can also use it here in this component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 325.38,
          "end": 328.98,
          "en": "And that's not something you can normally do in React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 328.98,
          "end": 332.28,
          "en": "but you can do it with server components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 332.28,
          "end": 336.09000000000003,
          "en": "So here we can then await the call to get meals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 336.09000000000003,
          "end": 338.383,
          "en": "to get the meals data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 338.383,
          "end": 342,
          "en": "and we'll get back our meals here just like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 342,
          "end": 343.92,
          "en": "that without useEffect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 343.92,
          "end": 347.103,
          "en": "without any unnecessary fetch request being sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 348.39,
          "end": 349.717,
          "en": "And with that done, we can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 349.717,
          "end": 352.83,
          "en": "therefore then use these meals down here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 352.83,
          "end": 354.69,
          "en": "where we have that MealsGrid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 354.69,
          "end": 358.017,
          "en": "We can simply pass meals to MealsGrid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 359.49,
          "end": 362.82,
          "en": "And with all that done, if you save everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 362.82,
          "end": 367.14,
          "en": "and you restart that development server, you should be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 367.14,
          "end": 372.033,
          "en": "to reload this meals page and see all those meals here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 373.38,
          "end": 376.08,
          "en": "Now, just a brief note, at this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 376.08,
          "end": 379.95,
          "en": "I had a tiny error in my styles when I recorded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 379.95,
          "end": 382.98,
          "en": "these videos, which is why for me,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 382.98,
          "end": 385.683,
          "en": "the meals look the way they do on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 386.55,
          "end": 388.8,
          "en": "For you, they should look like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 388.8,
          "end": 392.52,
          "en": "because I fixed that styling error in the attachment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 392.52,
          "end": 394.29,
          "en": "Now, besides that, nothing changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 394.29,
          "end": 396.27,
          "en": "It was just a styling error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 396.27,
          "end": 398.43,
          "en": "I just wanted to mention it here so",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 398.43,
          "end": 401.13,
          "en": "that you're not wondering why you have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 401.13,
          "end": 404.163,
          "en": "those extra titles here and I don't have them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 406.35,
          "end": 409.35,
          "en": "Now navigating to their details will work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 409.35,
          "end": 411.15,
          "en": "but will not show you anything of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 411.15,
          "end": 413.22,
          "en": "because we haven't added that logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 413.22,
          "end": 415.17,
          "en": "But you can see those meals here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
